# Conformance probe pack for rulings 23 and 26 of spec 0.8, most significant
# bit first. Public. No message kinds.
#
#   byte 0      n
#   byte 1      presence p.1 and p.2, then 6 unused bits
#   p.1, and p.2 is 0:  a count in 8 bits and that many recs; an item is a
#               kind byte, 1 small (x in 8 bits) or 0 tiny
#   p.2         a count in 8 bits and that many recs; an item is a kind byte,
#               2 wide (x in 16 bits) or 0 none
#
# The list recs is mapped by two groups that sit in different `if` blocks
# (ruling 23). Encode sets both bits for a list with items, so it writes the
# second form only; an item that was decoded as `small` or `tiny` then names
# a kind the second group does not have, and selects by `requires` (ruling 26).
format     conformance-seq-rulings-lists
version    0.8.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
field   probe.n  8  uint
presence p 2
pad 6
if p.1 !p.2
  group  probe.recs count 8
    kind   small
    when   8  1
    requires probe.x
    field  probe.x  8  uint
    kind   tiny
    when   8  0
  end
end
if p.2
  group  probe.recs count 8
    kind   wide
    when   8  2
    requires probe.x
    field  probe.x  16  uint
    kind   none
    when   8  0
  end
end
